{
  "case_id": "2009-08-1402",
  "document_hash": "469fd9c940b27a348d7689f7424a54f601c3572443d24cbc7fed4e41158a92b3",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1402",
      "confidence": 0.96,
      "document_hash": "469fd9c940b27a348d7689f7424a54f601c3572443d24cbc7fed4e41158a92b3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-469fd9c940b2-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 10:14 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1402",
      "confidence": 0.94,
      "document_hash": "469fd9c940b27a348d7689f7424a54f601c3572443d24cbc7fed4e41158a92b3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-469fd9c940b2-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The issue was whether the Michigan Supreme Court unreasonably applied clearly established Supreme Court precedent in rejecting Mr. Smith's claim that his jury was not drawn from a fair cross-section of the community."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1402",
      "confidence": 0.93,
      "document_hash": "469fd9c940b27a348d7689f7424a54f601c3572443d24cbc7fed4e41158a92b3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-469fd9c940b2-0000-0002",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And the percentage of African-Americans that appeared in the venires during that time period was -- they comprised 6 percent of the venires, where the jury-eligible population was 7.28 percent."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1402",
      "confidence": 0.92,
      "document_hash": "469fd9c940b27a348d7689f7424a54f601c3572443d24cbc7fed4e41158a92b3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-469fd9c940b2-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 7,
        "start": 7
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE STEVENS: May I interrupt with this question that goes both to what Justice Ginsburg asked and the other? Should we treat all areas the same, depending -- say it's -- the disparity between a jurisdiction which has only 3 or 4 percent of a minority should be treated similarly to a jurisdiction where they have 30 or 40 percent?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice STEVENS",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1402",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "469fd9c940b27a348d7689f7424a54f601c3572443d24cbc7fed4e41158a92b3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-469fd9c940b2-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But -- but there\u2019s a much higher percentage of African-Americans in Grand Rapids than there is in the county as a whole."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. RESTUCCIA",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1402",
      "confidence": 0.94,
      "document_hash": "469fd9c940b27a348d7689f7424a54f601c3572443d24cbc7fed4e41158a92b3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-469fd9c940b2-0001-0001",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "All of the district courts -- Grand Rapids, Rockford, all of these small municipalities -- drew from the circuit court pool."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice SCALIA",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1402",
      "confidence": 0.96,
      "document_hash": "469fd9c940b27a348d7689f7424a54f601c3572443d24cbc7fed4e41158a92b3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-469fd9c940b2-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Do you have to be a -- a resident of the district in order to serve as a juror in the district court?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. RESTUCCIA",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1402",
      "confidence": 0.98,
      "document_hash": "469fd9c940b27a348d7689f7424a54f601c3572443d24cbc7fed4e41158a92b3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-469fd9c940b2-0001-0003",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Yes."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice KENNEDY",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1402",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "469fd9c940b27a348d7689f7424a54f601c3572443d24cbc7fed4e41158a92b3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-469fd9c940b2-0001-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 27,
        "start": 27
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "If a procedure routinely results in statistical underrepresentation that is significant, is that not a clear showing of systematic exclusion?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice ROBERTS",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1402",
      "confidence": 0.94,
      "document_hash": "469fd9c940b27a348d7689f7424a54f601c3572443d24cbc7fed4e41158a92b3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-469fd9c940b2-0001-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 37,
        "start": 37
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Where -- where in the record is it established that Grand Rapids had a disproportionate need for jurors from the pool?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. RESTUCCIA",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1402",
      "confidence": 0.92,
      "document_hash": "469fd9c940b27a348d7689f7424a54f601c3572443d24cbc7fed4e41158a92b3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-469fd9c940b2-0001-0007",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 37,
        "start": 37
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I don't believe either side established that."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1402",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "469fd9c940b27a348d7689f7424a54f601c3572443d24cbc7fed4e41158a92b3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-469fd9c940b2-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: What's -- what's unreasonable about that argument?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1402",
      "confidence": 0.85,
      "document_hash": "469fd9c940b27a348d7689f7424a54f601c3572443d24cbc7fed4e41158a92b3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-469fd9c940b2-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Assume that there is an -- an identifiable disparity of 2 percent or 3 percent, or whatever it might be to get to the threshold of being significant, that\u2019s entirely caused by the fact that the members of the minority have personal excuses that justify non-service. What do you do with that case? Do you find that it was -- it\u2019s unconstitutional, or don't you?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1402",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "469fd9c940b27a348d7689f7424a54f601c3572443d24cbc7fed4e41158a92b3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-469fd9c940b2-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: Well, that's policy. Can't you say that that is systematic exclusion because it's part of the system?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1402",
      "confidence": 0.85,
      "document_hash": "469fd9c940b27a348d7689f7424a54f601c3572443d24cbc7fed4e41158a92b3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-469fd9c940b2-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 47,
        "start": 47
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: Are there -- are there courts that you know of that do what you are suggesting needs to be done? When a juror does not show up, the judge issues a bench warrant, and -- and the police are sent out to arrest the person and drag the person into court, or somebody says, I am a single parent, and I have children, and I'm too poor to have a nanny or an au pair, and, therefore, please excuse me; and they say, no, you have to find some way of getting here. Are there courts that do that?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1402",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "469fd9c940b27a348d7689f7424a54f601c3572443d24cbc7fed4e41158a92b3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-469fd9c940b2-0002-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 50,
        "start": 50
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Where is that in the record?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1402",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "469fd9c940b27a348d7689f7424a54f601c3572443d24cbc7fed4e41158a92b3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-469fd9c940b2-0002-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 51,
        "start": 51
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: Can we go back to your point about -- that there was a big change when the draw came from the circuit first, before the districts. I thought it was agreed that, before, there was an 18 percent, on average, comparative difference and, after, 15 percent. That doesn't sound like a big change."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1402",
      "confidence": 0.0,
